  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Building Tiny Houses for villages in Kherson and Mykolaiv for particularly vulnerable people</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project will provide Tiny Houses for families in 4 villages in Kherson and Mykolaiv region who have suffered massive destruction during the war. A Tiny House is a module-based concept house. It is 18 m2, small, but fully functional with interior to fit 2 adults and 2 children. The house is provided with appliances for water connections and electricity, when this is suitable for the receiver. Otherwise, the house is adapted to fit living conditions without these and will for instance have a stove for wood instead.  
CRD will collaborate with local Baptist church community, heads of 4 villages, a social worker, a project manager and professional house-building team and the 15 targeted families.
Main activities are procuring materials and assembling module-based Tiny Houses and delivering the Tiny Houses to each family.
The expected outcome of this intervention is improved security and living conditions of vulnerable people and families in Kherson and Mykolaiv region</narrative>
  </description>
